< **RN5 — REGARD IS SPARSE, EVENT-BORN, TWO-SIGNED, BANDED, WITH ONE PLAIN REASON.** An actor feels something about a subject only when an AUTHORED seed (the DM's allies-and-enemies list; a champion's authored relations) or a DEED it has heard of creates it; nothing is pre-populated. A regard holds two signs apart (warmth and grudge, the `factionPairStates` idiom, so "loved and hated" is expressible on scrutiny) and reads as one band on the seven-word ladder (§2.4); every change keeps ONE dominant reason in the world's words (the typed incident, concern 9b). Each holder tracks at most a capped number of EMERGENT subjects (DRAFT 12, UNMEASURED); the DM's seeds and sets (`declared`, `dmSet`) are exempt from the cap and from eviction; the weakest emergent subject — the one whose strongest decayed term is smallest — drops first. A town's or a court's feeling about ANOTHER town or court is never an RN entry: it is the landed pair state (`relationshipState`; law E14), and RN's writer refuses such a pair. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r1) — RN-r1-16: weakness defined and the DM's hand never evicted; RN-r1-1: no second pair-regard beside `relationshipState`.]
