< **RN9 — EVERY ACTOR READS A DEED THROUGH TWO LENSES.** A deed's INHERENT VALUE is derived from its kind and its target on the landed alignment axes (kindness and lawfulness, plus aggressiveness as the third coordinate) — never a second judgment the DM must make (§6). Lens one: what the act is, read through the holder's own alignment. Lens two: whom it helped or hurt, read through the holder's friends and rivals — for a town or a court, FIRST its LANDED relationship with the town the deed helped or hurt (`relationshipState`: `rival · cold_war · hostile · allied …`, with trust and resentment); for a person or the party, RN's regard link. PERSONALITY sets the mix (the landed trait adjectives); a holder with no tie to anyone the deed touched judges the act alone. A good or neutral rival grumbles and holds nothing against the doer; an unambiguously evil rival keeps the grudge; an evil holder with no tie shrugs at a kindness and holds no grudge; condemning a deed good on its face without a reason costs the condemner its own people's regard (one bounded term, never legitimacy); an ambiguous act reads NEUTRAL until the DM marks it. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r1) — RN-r1-1 (RULINGS-ROUND1 RN-r1-1, executed): lens two reads the landed rivalry first · RN-r1-3: evil shrugs at kindness · RN-r1-8: the mix keys on landed traits.] A TOWN's character enters lens one only as the alignment axes' LANDED BANDS (`lawWordFor`, `natureWordFor`) and never through the aggression drive, so the host's catalogued alignment defects can move a town's reading only across a band edge (§6.2) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — HOST-r1-7 (RULINGS-ROUND1 ADDENDUM, as worded)].
