lTick > now) never age"). A row that declares neither is relayed exactly as a feed seed (both leaks). THE FINDINGS ROW declares both: `relayedTick` = the seed's tick, and `arrivalTick` = the seed's tick + the relay's OWN price from the meeting town to the seat — 0 when they are one town (`distanceRead.js :: hopWeeks`: "same settlement ⇒ 0"), else the relay's `travelTicks` line exactly, `Math.max(1, finiteNumber(hopWeeks(digest, meetingId, seatId, season), 1))` (no second speed for news) — so the report reaches the home court ALONE, a carry's weeks after the meeting, and lives there its `notable` thirteen weeks from its arrival. EXECUTED (`cure/D-RN-r4-probe/r4Probe.out.json` A, on the verifier's five-town graph): the cured seed is held by `home` only, visible from tick 11 (a one-week carry), gone at tick 25; the round-3 text's seed (origin the meeting town, the guard unstamped) reached all five towns; a row declaring neither field relays as a feed seed [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — RN-r3-verify FAIL ("RN's seed is held by `fourth, home, meet, post, third`, which includes the post that was spied on. CH's seed is held by `home` only") and its ROUTED-UNAPPLIED (a)–(c) (`cure/D-CH-r3.md` §5 RN), under RULINGS-ROUND4 A.9 ("COPIES a row's declared `relayedTick` onto the seed … the findings' origin is the EMPLOYER'S SEAT; the leak `eventRef` gains `:<retainer.sinceTick>`; the seed's `arrivalTick = tick + hopWeeks(meeting, seat, season)`"); the round-3 bracket's "`relayedTick: null` … relays it exactly as a feed seed" holds only for a row that declares no guard]. The arm copies only the structured content fields the row DECLARES (`captureContent`'s law: "ONLY structured fields are copied"; each declared field is a persisted rumor-ledger field whose lifecycle row is its OWNER's — CH's; BD's), and never writes a person, the party or a body into `partyIds`. A registered telling carries no `deed:` eventRef, so RN's heard pass (§5.1) never reads it: it moves no fame, no regard and no credibility; its OWNER's pass reads its arrivals (CH's `paragonBeliefs`; BD's for its row). Its belief-map refresh through `reportsBySubject` is its owner's flag's disclosed shift (CH's `paragonCovertEnabled`; BD's), never RN's. Host: zero further lines — the list is read inside `renown/deedTelling.js`, so CH's ≤ 3-line fallback in `rumorNetwork.js` is not needed (PLAUSIBLE until CH-7's car-0 measures that each row's inputs stand on `worldState` at the rumor stage, the tick after CH's pass wrote them). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — D-CH-r2 §5.2(d): CH's leak (§9) and findings (§8) named RN's telling arm as their seeding seam, PLAUSIBLE until RN's arm took a registered source; it now takes them, by a closed list.]
