< **Reads:** BELIEF — the version of a deed that reached the holder's town (the rumor ledger's record for `deed:<deedId>` at that settlement, its visible parts by the read model's completeness thresholds), or, in the omniscient arm, the deed itself inside its WHOLE projected reach (`heardAt`, §4.3 — never the decayed ring [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — RN-V1]). A person holder hears what the town it STANDS IN has heard (the npcLedger `residency`/`placed` host; R1 RF-6). A CORPS holder (`u:`) hears what the town its unit stands at has heard — the node its free unit's position names (WC §1.7.2's army-style stepper, read as `armyTransit.js :: currentRegion`: "the node at its position along the path (rounded to the nearest hop)"; PLAUSIBLE until WC-10 lands, named at CH-10's car) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-6]. A NAMED GANG holder (`g:`) hears what its HOME has heard — `homeId` (BD §2.2: "its tie town"), else the anchor town of its base site (`baseSiteId`), else the settlement of the country it stands in (`where.ids[0]`): "the deeds heard at its home" (BD §2.1) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — BD's routes]. **Writes:** `spatialLedgers.regard` only, through `regardLedger.js :: writeHeardTerm({ worldState, holderKey, subjectKey, deedId, ver, mag, reading, tick })` — the ONE writer; it replaces the holder's term for that deed (or for the deed it corrects) and never adds a second (RN6). **The pass:** `renown/regardHeard.js :: advanceHeardRegard({ worldState, tick })` scans each settlement's rumor ledger for `deed:` tellings whose VERSION — THE TRIPLE (`ver`, `mag`, the heard doer) — differs from the holder's stored term (an arrival; a better telling superseding — `mergeArrival` keeps the earliest `arrivalTick`, so "arrived this tick" alone would miss a better version, and `pickBetterTelling` supersedes on CONTINUOUS completeness first (`if (a.completeness01 !== b.completeness01) return a.completeness01 > b.completeness01 ? a : b;`), so a better telling ma